  "body": "Instead of having the constructor throw a SecurityError this will\nresult in a network error that will be reported as an error event on\nthe Worker/SharedWorker instance.\n\nAlthough it seems like this change removes support for data URLs, that\nin fact already happened when Fetch was integrated and we did not set\nthe same-origin data-URL flag. Which is in line with Chrome and the\nstated goals of at least one Firefox engineer.\n",
